### AON -> Agent conversion webhook: retry vectors
### The event id and raw body are unchanged. Each retry has a fresh timestamp
### and signature. The receiver evaluates idempotency separately from signature.

| Attempt | Timestamp | X-AON-Signature |
|---:|---:|---|
| 1 | 1776450600 | 8b0d7aa29c9717dc0fdcb278237050d6a5c1ca816ad0b6560b8240722304a5b8 |
| 2 (+1 min) | 1776450660 | 58472d51cda98f5e1581c802d8431da4b52c7e3a790868c7f2e4a9e375619f71 |
| 3 (+5 min) | 1776450960 | 952b81e39c64ddedbc6d3ad31282886d828b19ac985131536519ba0ac20dce13 |
| 4 (+30 min) | 1776452760 | a1ece7e2542441d506957a578a97f155893f7bb8a03d0f5db8b5c5ca144c5973 |
| 5 (+2 h) | 1776459960 | 97ad856154e3519499879147994a52e8649f8976dec9b083f1897ce252ed1ea0 |

Each vector uses the same `POST /webhook/aon/conversion?source=aon&delivery=conversion`
request target, `X-AON-Key: aon_cb_v2`, and raw JSON body as
`basic-conversion.http`.

Expected receiver results:

1. The first valid vector may apply the business side effect.
2. A later identical-body vector returns 2xx without a second side effect.
3. Reusing the same key with a different raw body returns HTTP 409.
4. A non-2xx or timeout is retried only through Attempt 5; a 2xx stops delivery.
